Getting Started Guide - For Developers
------
Welcome to the world of E-comOS!
Come into a new community, you have many thing want to know, right? This guide will give you some helps for your works!
------
How to Contribute
One. Submit an Issue Report
  If you found out a bug, you can submit one bug report to our bug tracker, when you submit the report, you write these in your report:
         - What were you doing when the problem occurred?
         - What did you expect to happen?
         - What actually happened?
         - What operating system are you using?
         - What CPU architecture are you using?
         - What version of the kernel are you using?
         - What version of the compiler are you using?
         - Or , can you submit the screenshot with your report?
  We'll fix your problem quickly, but some problems we won't fix, because may be it's yourself or your computer's problem.
  If we encounter this situation, we will mark your issue report as "WONTFIX," meaning we will not fix the issue.
Two. Translate
  There are some comments in codes, some documents or others using English only , or other language only.
  We need some people to translate them, if you're going to translate, please `git clone` our repo first, and send a patch to our mailing list.
Three. Codes
  The codes is most important, if you can, please join up us to develop E-comOS, we're using 1TBS, 4-bits tab and snake_case only.
  We'll reject use the Allman, GNU style and spaces, camlCase codes in our codes.
  E-comOS unsupport the pull request via GitHub, please use the mailing list.
  A. Vibe Code
    Coder can use the AI to help they. But, you've to know, if you want to use the AI(vibe code), you MUST:
       - Review your code by yourself;
       - CAN'T send the patch and using AI to provide responses during code reviews;
       - You CAN'T use the AI to generate the ideas; and
       - The copyright is YOURs, when you push the code, your copyright line should like this:
                Copyright(C) YOUR NAME   YEARS
Four. Douments
  We talked the codes, but we forgot documents.
  In the E-comOS Operating System Project, we often use the MarkDown or paint text.
  A.Paint Text
    When you want to write documents for E-comOS and you're using the paint text, please remember:
    The length of a line of characters is 16 centimeters.
    If your line is too long, the reader can't read your document's full text. It's very bad.
  (NOTICE: We know there are so many kinds of English, but we don't cares which one you're using)
  B.Markdown
    I hate the Markdown.
    Because when you type the Enter key, if you DO NOT add the `<br>`, Markdown cannot switch the line , in the preview ... it's looks a shit.
    So, please add the `<br>` before `enter` key.
